  "title": "Model Bake-off — Cohere vs. incumbents",
  "widgets": [
    {
      "definition": {
        "background_color": "transparent",
        "content": "**The Cohere bake-off — one pane over the three seat comparisons** (RC1-477; data producers RC1-473/474/475).\n\nStanding verdicts, 2026-09-29: **embedding seat — OpenAI keeps it** (near-tie, rerank net-neutral) · **generation seat — Haiku keeps it** (Command ~1.8× faster but 2× verbose, 2 judged fails) · **reviewer seat — Claude keeps it** (Command lost recall/categorisation; `tool_choice` unsupported).\n\n**Read the numbers with three caveats.** (1) Cohere *eval-run* spans include the 6.5 s trial-key pacing sleep inside the span, and eval spans join the production ml_app/service — span-duration latency for Command is inflated until unpaced production traffic exists; the APM p50 widgets are honest per-call latency. (2) `command-a-plus-05-2026` has **no published per-token price**, so cost widgets show the priced arms only — the illustrative Command figure lives in RC1-475. (3) Retrieval gauges post once per eval run: \"no data\" on a short window is cadence, not outage.",
        "font_size": "14",
        "has_padding": true,
        "text_align": "left",
        "type": "note"
      },
      "id": 3984080444898818
    },
