      "definition": {
        "layout_type": "ordered",
        "title": "Reviewer seat — pr-review-agent (RC1-474: Claude keeps the seat)",
        "type": "group",
        "widgets": [
          {
            "definition": {
              "background_color": "transparent",
              "content": "**The Command arm never reaches LLM Obs** — it ran through `pr_agent/evals/cohere.py` against the pinned 13-case subset, and both arms live in the eval store (`pr-review-20260930T023659.389030Z` Claude, `pr-review-20260930T025623.132938Z` Command). Claude: recall 10/10, categorisation 10/10, $0.0447/review. Command: 9/10, 8/10, unpriced (~$0.0716 illustrative), decoy precision 2/2 vs Claude 1/2 — but `tool_choice` unsupported (~9% prose answers) and nondeterministic `422 INVALID_TOOL_GENERATION`. The cost gap is a caching story: no prompt cache on Cohere, while Claude serves ~78% of context at 0.1× cache-read. Widgets below are the Claude production arm only.",
              "font_size": "14",
              "has_padding": true,
              "text_align": "left",
              "type": "note"
            },
            "id": 5880135060221358
          },
